WF-51 — Send Slack Message

## Summary

- Inputs: channelId (Slack channel ID), messageText (plain text only — no blocks / attachments supported in this utility)
- Outputs: Message posted to the given Slack channel; Slack API response returned to caller (includes message_ts)
- State Transitions: none
- Calls Sub-Workflows: none
- **Notes:**
  - Text-only utility. Callers needing rich Slack formatting (blocks, attachments) should extend WF-51 with optional fields rather than bypassing it. Outbound Slack posts are NOT logged to chinmay_astro.messages (intentional — message_log table audits WhatsApp traffic only).

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by another workflow with { channelId, messageText } passed through.
Step 2: Post to Slack via Slack API (chat.postMessage) using the Slack credential — channel=<channelId>, text=<messageText>. Go to Step 3.
Step 3: End (response from Slack returned to caller).
